BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191157@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260622T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260622T190000
SUMMARY:TEDxBoston: Visions of the Next 250 - A First Look
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are
  Confirmed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191157\n\n5
 :30PM Reception\, 6:00PM Discussion \nFor 250 years\, Massachusetts has b
 een a place where bold ideas take root. On June 22nd\, the evening before 
 the Visions of the Next 250 gathering at GBH\, we invite members to a priv
 ate preview in The Reading Room to explore a more challenging question: wh
 at will the next 250 years look like\, and who is shaping them?\n\nJohn We
 rner\, venture capitalist\, MIT lecturer\, and Forbes AI columnist\, will 
 interview four people working at the frontier of science\, medicine\, educ
 ation\, ethics\, and intelligence in the kind of off-the-record conversati
 on that needs fewer chairs to go deeper.\n\nTogether\, they will explore s
 ome of the defining questions of our time: where machine intelligence is h
 eaded and what it asks of us\; how wearable technology and data are transf
 orming our understanding of health\, resilience\, and human performance\; 
 how society can thoughtfully navigate the ethical challenges that accompan
 y powerful new technologies\; and how education and lifelong learning must
  evolve to prepare future generations for a world increasingly shaped by i
 nnovation and artificial intelligence.\n\nSpeakers include:\n\nAlham Saada
 t - Executive Director\, The Innovation Trail of Greater Boston\nAlex Wiss
 ner-Gross - Investor & Entrepreneur\nEmily Capodilupo - Senior Vice Presid
 ent of Research\, Algorithms\, and Data\, WHOOP\nJoseph Aoun - President\,
  Northeastern University\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for 
 members\, plus one guest. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191157
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
