BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-192120@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260626T100000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260626T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260626T113000
SUMMARY:Coffee & Conversation: Inclusion in a Divided World with Lord John 
 Mann 
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 14 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1
 92120\n\n10:00AM Reception\, 10:30AM Discussion \nAs Boston comes togethe
 r with the global community this summer through events such as the FIFA Wo
 rld Cup and Tall Ships\, there is no better time to reflect on collective 
 inclusion and efforts to diminish discrimination.\n\nIn this special editi
 on of Coffee & Conversation\, join Lord John Mann\, the United Kingdom Gov
 ernment's Independent Adviser on Antisemitism\, and Colette Phillips\, Pre
 sident and CEO of Colette Phillips Communications and founder of Get Konne
 cted!\, for a timely discussion on inclusion\, discrimination\, and the ch
 allenges facing democratic societies today.\n\nLord Mann has led groundbre
 aking initiatives to combat hate in sport\, delivering educational program
 s to thousands across professional football clubs and creating recognized 
 Jewish Supporters Groups that promote inclusion and belonging. Drawing on 
 his experience in government\, sport\, and civil society\, Lord Mann will 
 offer valuable insights on building stronger and more resilient communitie
 s.\n\nTogether\, Lord Mann and Colette Phillips will explore how instituti
 ons\, communities\, and individuals can help build more inclusive societie
 s\, confront prejudice\, and foster meaningful dialogue in an increasingly
  complex world.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members o
 nly. Light bites and refreshments will be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/192120
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
