BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-191168@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260714T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260714T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260714T190000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Man Made" with Karen Korellis Reuther
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free\nAvailability: 33 spots lef
 t\nStatus: Available\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/1
 91168\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Discussion\nWhat if the world around us
  wasn't designed with everyone in mind?\n\nJoin us for an illuminating con
 versation with Karen Korellis Reuther - designer\, educator\, inclusion ad
 vocate\, and author of the forthcoming book MAN-MADE: How We Designed a Wo
 rld That Leaves Women Out\, and How We Can Make It Right. Drawing on more 
 than four decades of experience\, including leadership roles at Nike and R
 eebok and her current work at Harvard's Graduate School of Design\, Karen 
 explores the hidden ways gender bias has been built into the products\, sy
 stems\, and spaces we encounter every day.\n\nFrom personal protective equ
 ipment and athletic footwear to healthcare\, transportation\, and public i
 nfrastructure\, MAN-MADE reveals how design decisions rooted in a male def
 ault continue to shape women's experiences\, often with profound consequen
 ces. Through compelling research\, real-world examples\, and a forward-loo
 king vision for change\, Karen invites us to reconsider the world we have 
 inherited - and imagine one designed for everyone.\n\n*This event is compl
 imentary and reserved for members only. Light bites and refreshments will 
 be served.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/191168
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
